WEBVTT

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.310
I see...

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.820
So you can stay on Itogami Island 
without any fear, huh?

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.120
That's great, Yume.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.520
Yes!

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.540
Thanks to that rude young man over there,

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.730
I have someone to take care of me, too.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.570
Hey, now.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.580
So wait for me, okay?

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.040
Huh? Wait for what?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.840
You... promised me, didn't you?

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.870
That you'd make me happy 
for the rest of my life...

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.060
I'll try my hardest at everything I do!

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.030
Wait, that wasn't what I meant by that...

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.180
What? You didn't mean it?

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.780
Officer! We've got a scammer over here!

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.260
Hey! Yaze!

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.440
For crying out loud... 
What in the world is he doing?

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.610
What about you, Yukina-chan? 
What are <i>you</i> doing?

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.160
If there's something you 
want to say to Kojou-kun,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.240
just march right up and tell him.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.740
I couldn't just barge 
into the restaurant, though...

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.280
Why not?

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.090
I don't think that's 
anything to worry about.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.370
Do you, Kanon-chan?

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:09.850
I... sort of understand 
how Yukina-chan feels.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.070
Really?

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.800
I mean, that's fine, though.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.510
It's kinda fun seeing you 
like this, Yukina-chan.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.190
Um...

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.770
I'm sorry for dragging you both into this.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.200
It's okay.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:28.730
I've always thought it was fun 
to watch them all together like this.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.020
Man, it's hot.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.880
I'm gonna go get something to drink.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.310
Come with me, Kanon-chan.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.990
What do you want, Yukina-chan?

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:40.300
Uh... I'll have a cold green tea, then.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.040
Okay, got it!

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:49.920
Excuse me, little miss middle schooler.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.260
Is that bench free?

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.650
Oh, yes, it is. Help yourself.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:57.910
Thanks.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:59.880
Whew, what a relief.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:07.440
So, what is a middle school girl 
like you to Akatsuki Kojou, huh?

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.390
Huh?!

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:13.120
Well, you've been giving 
Kojou a hell of a death glare.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:18.060
I thought maybe you were... 
you know, jealous or something.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.070
Am I right?

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.740
You are not!

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:25.590
I-I'm merely observing him! 
I'm not jealous at all!

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:29.010
Observing... Observing, eh?

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.790
Is that what you call 
stalking a one-sided crush?

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:33.800
Excuse me?!

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.870
"Observing"! I love it! 
Ah, to be young again!

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.230
Damn, that's so bittersweet!

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:41.410
Why are we even discussing this?!

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:44.100
Actually, first of all, who <i>are</i> you?!

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.820
Gajou-kun?!

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.100
Oh, hey, Nagisa.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.690
Shit! It's really you!

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.600
Why are you here, you lousy father?!

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.200
Father?

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.810
Y-You're Akatsuki-senpai's...

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.620
father?!

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:07.600
I'm Kojou and Nagisa's 
father, Akatsuki Gajou.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:08.950
Nice to meet ya.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.010
So hot...

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.500
Hey, Natsuki-chan, today—ow!

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:52.850
Don't call your teacher "chan" when she's 
already irritable from this stinking heat, idiot.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.670
Today is New Year's Eve, right?

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.200
Yes, that it is.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.360
So why am I stuck here taking 
supplementary lessons right now?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:10.170
Ask a certain idiot who failed his 
make-up exam due to his unexcused absence.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.720
Astarte.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:12.920
Accept.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.630
Are you being snarky?!

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:18.610
By the way, Akatsuki...

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:22.310
Where is your father right now?

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.410
He's not on Itogami Island.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.320
I mean, not that he ever is,

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.380
but right now, he's visiting 
the mainland with my sister.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:30.260
What?

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:33.920
Well, actually, about... a week ago?

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.160
He just suddenly showed up

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.140
and said he was taking Nagisa 
to see our grandma in Tanzawa.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.400
Tanzawa... hmm...

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:43.730
I see.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:47.670
Hang on, Natsuki-chan... 
Do you know my dad?

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:49.280
Unfortunately.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.950
Akatsuki Gajou made 
a nuisance of himself many times

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.940
while I was working my other job.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.610
He did come in handy 
on rare occasions, though.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.600
Your attack mage job?

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.670
What the hell was that old jerk doing?

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.420
Can you contact him?

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:05.680
I'm not sure.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:08.330
The area around Lake Kannawa,

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:11.760
where my grandma lives, 
has really spotty cell service.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.940
Why do you ask, though?

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.440
Did you have business with him?

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.870
No, I was just a bit curious,

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.200
for whatever reason.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:25.840
We are aliens...

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:33.450
Himeragi?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.630
Y-Yes?

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.490
I'm leaving a change of clothes here. 
They're Nagisa's, but they should work.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.500
Okay, thank you.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.720
Thank you for letting me use the bath.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.570
Sorry to make you help 
with the end-of-the-year cleaning.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.800
Well, I had to.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.720
If you'd been left to do it all alone,

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.520
it wouldn't have been done 
before the year ended.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.520
Damn it. What was my stupid mother thinking,

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:02.020
with her "If you want New Year's money, 
you gotta clean! Hee hee!" line?

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:07.150
It's not like she cares about New Year's. 
She works through it like every other day.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:10.280
I'll get the New Year's soba ready.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:13.420
You can have your bath in the meantime.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.880
Minamiya-sensei said that?

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:25.380
Yeah. She seemed concerned 
about my dad and Nagisa.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:30.080
Come to think of it, it's been 
a week now since they left.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.900
Have you heard anything from Nagisa-chan?

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:33.850
Nope.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.170
You haven't, either?

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:37.510
No.

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:40.700
I see... Not even a word to you...

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.990
Hey, Kojou. I came to see ya.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.880
What're you doing here at this hour?

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:50.320
What're you talking about?

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.220
We said we'd all do the first 
shrine visit of the year together.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.710
Crap! Sorry, I totally forgot!

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:57.250
Where's everyone else?

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.790
They should be here soon.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:00.820
There.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.000
What are you guys wearing?

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.840
W-Well, it's New Year's.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.690
We thought it'd be nice 
to dress up for a change.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:28.650
Do we look okay, Onii-san?

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:32.370
But it's crazy to wear long sleeves like 
that in this island's climate!

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:33.400
Current Temperature

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.400
Are you okay?!

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.560
W-We're fine.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.870
As long as we can get some water...

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.340
Here's some water for everyone. 
Please help yourselves.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:47.810
Yukina-chan?

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.810
Fitting in quite naturally 
at Kojou's place, aren't you?

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:55.160
Oh, um... Nagisa-chan 
is away visiting family,

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:58.690
so I was helping with his end-of-the-year 
cleaning and New Year's soba.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:09.900
Look at you two, fresh out of the bath 
and smelling like the same shampoo...

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.630
Wait! You didn't actually get in together—

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:14.480
The hell are you saying?!

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.070
There's a child here!

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.530
Man, that hurt!

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.340
It was just a little joke to lighten things up!

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:22.650
Anyway...

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:24.940
Himeragi and I are gonna get ready now,

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:26.300
so sit tight for a bit.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:28.230
Oh, right... The air conditioner...

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.640
I just turned it down.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:32.890
Thanks, Himeragi.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.460
They're just like newlyweds.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:39.170
Motoki, this heat is making me 
irritable enough as it is.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:41.890
Why don't ya go to his room 
to change with him, then?

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:49.080
It's from Nagisa. She finally—

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:50.770
This is...

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:55.380
A magic circle?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.520
Three!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:00.490
Two!

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:01.450
One!

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:04.430
Zero!

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.380
Happy New Year!

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:07.590
Happy New Year!

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.130
Hey, Kojou, why are you making that face?

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:15.290
We don't know for sure 
that anything happened to Nagisa-chan.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:18.830
I know! I'm not worried or anything!

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:20.510
Yeah, right.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:25.720
Itogami Shrine
Happy New Year

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.990
Well, go ahead and say a prayer.

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:25.440
They say prayers offered 
at this shrine are granted.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:35.980
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.200
<b>Bad</b>

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.200
<b></b>Luck

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.510
One more try!

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.700
<b>Worst</b>

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.700
<b></b>Luck

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:48.640
Onii-san...

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.620
<b>Best</b>

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.620
<b>Luck</b>

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.630
Want to trade for mine?

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.550
I-It's fine!

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:56.230
If you're at your lowest now, 
that means it can't get any worse!

00:10:56.230 --> 00:11:01.140
Yeah. Maybe the unluckier you are, 
the luckier Nagisa-chan will be!

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:08.560
She's not gonna end up telling us this 
was just fireworks, is she?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.150
I really doubt that,

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.570
but digital data can be 
altered in all sorts of ways.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:16.970
You shouldn't dwell on it so much.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:20.650
Hey, Himeragi...

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:23.230
If this is a magic circle,

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:25.980
do you know what kind 
of effect this type would have?

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:30.160
I'm sorry. Sayaka-san might 
know, but I can't say I do.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.620
Kirasaka?

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.040
Actually, this does look like...

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:38.590
...Sayaka-san's Koukarin, yes.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.750
Is there anyone else 
who has a bow like that?

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.220
No, they're difficult to use.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:47.710
I've heard Sayaka-san 
is the only one who's mastered it.

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:48.950
But...

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.460
I've also heard that there is 
a mass-produced model

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:55.330
that's been simplified 
to make it easier to use.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.760
It's only a rumor, though.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:59.080
I'll ask her myself.

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:01.920
Who's he calling?

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.500
Sayaka-san.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.960
She knows a lot about 
that type of magic circle.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:09.840
How does he know Kirasaka-san's number?

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:11.040
No idea...

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.790
She's not answering.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:16.880
In fact, it's telling me 
this number isn't in use.

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:18.810
Then Sayaka-san's cell phone—

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:20.140
Hey, Himeragi!

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.980
Is there any other way 
to get in touch with her?

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:24.080
Hey!

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:26.930
I know you're worried about Nagisa-chan,

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.940
but don't grab a girl like that!

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:31.490
Sorry, Himeragi. I wasn't thinking.

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:32.730
It's okay.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.520
I'm worried about Nagisa-chan, too.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:39.170
I guess I have no choice.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.450
What do you mean?

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.680
L-Listen, Kojou...

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:48.640
My parents are out tonight, 
so no one's home.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:51.750
Want to come over?

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:58.300
H-Huh?

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:07.920
There! That's Nagisa-chan 
and your dad, right?

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:09.680
The security cameras, huh?

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.430
I get it. 
This'll tell us where they're going.

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:18.270
Right, yes... Of course this 
is what she meant.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:19.030
About what?

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:21.340
Nothing! Never mind!

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.290
<i>Her dad rented a car at the airport...</i>

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:27.230
<i>using an alias.</i>

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.120
Why an alias?

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.200
The car left Haneda on the Metropolitan 
Expressway, bound for Tokyo...

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:35.130
But they stopped briefly 
just before Shibuya.

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:36.230
Shibuya?

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:39.970
<i>There's a record of them shopping 
at a second-hand clothes shop in Harajuku.</i>

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:42.440
<i>They also stopped to eat cake.</i>

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.630
Then they checked into a hotel, and...

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:47.930
What is this place? A strip bar?!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.140
Wait, with Nagisa?!

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:50.960
No, he's alone.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.610
That piece of shit!

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:55.770
<i>They spent the next day 
at an amusement park,</i>

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.360
<i>and they booked a hotel on the grounds.</i>

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:01.320
Is there any point in tracing all this stuff?

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:05.280
<i>Oh, it looks like they finally 
got serious the next day.</i>

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:06.800
Finally?

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:10.040
The date matches the one 
on Nagisa-chan's message.

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.020
That's weird.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:13.660
Do you see it, Mogwai?

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:14.560
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.240
Weird? What's weird?

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:19.090
They're moving around too smoothly.

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:23.520
It's New Year's, and they haven't 
gotten caught in traffic once.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:27.510
It's almost as if all the other cars 
are avoiding the route to Kannawa.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.920
Couldn't it just be a coincidence?

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:32.980
<i>Did someone put up 
a barrier to repel people?</i>

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:38.210
<i>But it would take a major organized effort 
to put up a barrier on this scale.</i>

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:41.120
<i>I get it. I figured out the trick.</i>

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.140
<i>The Self-Defense Force is behind it.</i>

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.630
<i>They're heading toward Kannawa Lake 
under the pretense of offering aid</i>

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.420
<i>in the wake of snowfall and landslides.</i>

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:48.610
The Self-Defense Force?

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:52.860
<i>But the group that's really 
pulling the strings is SDC,</i>

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:55.120
<i>also known as Sorcery Disaster Control.</i>

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.640
SDC?

00:14:57.570 --> 00:14:59.800
No... But why...

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:00.590
Himeragi?

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:01.890
What's wrong?

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.390
Excuse me!

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.280
Hey, Himeragi! Where are you going?!

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.190
Wait, Kojou!

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:14.640
Thanks, Asagi! You were a big help! 
I owe you dinner or something!

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:19.070
Jeez, what's going on?

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:23.020
Hey, Himeragi! What's gotten into you?

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.320
Don't follow me!

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:27.490
I need to know for sure.

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:29.760
Know what for sure?

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:35.420
SDC is one of the dummy organizations 
under the Lion King Organization.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:37.740
The Lion King Organization?

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.630
What's this about? It's called 
Sorcery Disaster Control, right?

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:45.430
So does that mean Nagisa 
was involved in a magic-related disaster?

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:47.870
Or they involved her in one...

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:50.850
Which is why I need to go find out for sure.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.470
At that antique shop?

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:56.390
The one where Cat-sensei 
and that Kirasaka puppet were?

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.560
I thought it was in this area...

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:07.560
The barrier spell has changed.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:09.990
Even I can't decode it now.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.740
If that's what they want...

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:15.310
Himeragi?

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.330
Senpai, please stay back here.

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:18.900
Schneesturm Wolfin!

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:25.990
That was a bit overboard...

00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:27.460
It's an emergency!

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:33.460
Looks like the shop's closed.

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:35.390
I guess it would be, since it's New Year's.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.530
Whoa, Himeragi!

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:46.850
Don't try to stop me!

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.250
Forget it! Just calm down!

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:49.180
Let go!

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:52.150
There's no point in going inside 
when no one's in there!

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:53.150
But...

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:56.030
If no one has told you anything,

00:16:56.030 --> 00:17:00.270
that must mean the Lion King Organization 
is deliberately keeping us out of the loop.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:02.740
That would explain Kirasaka's deal, too.

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.490
How can you be so calm right now?!

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:10.930
The Lion King Organization may have 
involved Nagisa-chan in something terrible!

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:14.060
I wouldn't say I'm all that calm.

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:14.960
But...

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:20.430
Organizations always have different 
factions vying for all the power.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:24.560
So if there's a side to the Lion 
King Organization that you don't know,

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.980
it's nothing you need 
to feel responsible for.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:28.480
Senpai...

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:33.110
Besides, there's no way 
Kirasaka would ever betray you.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.640
You're right...

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:40.530
I understand... so, Senpai...

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:44.080
I'd appreciate it if you'd let go of me now.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.300
Where do you think you're touching, anyway?

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:47.760
Oh, sorry!

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:52.420
No, it's fine. It was 
my fault to begin with.

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:57.320
But I guess we still don't know what 
the Lion King Organization's up to, huh?

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:58.880
So we're stuck.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:01.440
You seem troubled, Fourth Progenitor.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:04.850
Kisaki Kiriha!

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.200
I'm sorry to interrupt

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:09.570
when you were so boldly embracing 
on a street filled with love hotels

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:11.190
on the first day of the new year.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.930
Wha— I-It's not like that!

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:14.590
We weren't embracing!

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:16.840
What the hell do you want with us, anyway?!

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:18.630
You want to know what

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:23.370
the Lion King Organization 
is doing at Lake Kannawa, don't you?

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:26.830
I'm willing to tell you.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:32.830
Of course, once you find out, 
you may regret it.

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.720
Island Departure Exam Room

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:40.060
Okay, this will sting a little.

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:47.620
It's such a hassle going 
through this every time.

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:49.970
I know it's necessary, 
since we're in a demon district, but...

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:52.960
<i>You're one brave little miss,</i>

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:57.080
<i>going all the way to 
the mainland to help Kojou out.</i>

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:59.720
I'm not doing it for him, okay?!

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:02.950
My sister's on the mainland, 
and I want to see her again, too.

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.340
I just thought I'd check 
in on Nagisa-chan while I'm there.

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:06.090
<i>Oh?</i>

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:08.580
Just shut up, would you?! It's time to go!

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.620
Gate 4, right?

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.520
<i>We've got trouble. It's the Island Guard.</i>

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:14.660
What?

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:16.760
<i>They're after you, without a doubt.</i>

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.830
<i>You'll be fully surrounded 
in one minute and forty seconds.</i>

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:21.930
You've gotta be kidding!

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:25.360
<i>You can get out to the taxiway 
via a staircase sixty meters ahead.</i>

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:26.610
<i>Then it's all up to luck.</i>

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:30.820
Damn it! Why is this happening 
on the first day of the new year?!

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:34.600
You're sure you want to go with me?

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:37.810
I'm your observer, remember?

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:43.060
If you're leaving the island via illegal means 
with help from Minamiya-sensei,

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:45.250
of course I'm going with you.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:47.090
We'll be committing a crime, though.

00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:50.080
You're pointing that out <i>now</i>?

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:53.340
Good point.

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:59.760
Asagi's house is huge, 
too, but this is crazy.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.600
Happy New Year.

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:07.130
We already went through 
the New Year formalities!

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:08.350
And why are you naked?!

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:11.810
No, Astarte-san! 
You shouldn't run around like that!

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:20.480
Sorry...

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.100
W-Were you in the bath?

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:25.820
How long do you have to stare at them?

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:28.960
Senpai, you are such...

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:31.310
an indecent person!

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:31.290
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:36.640
Barging into someone's home

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:39.710
and making a molester of yourself 
on the first day of the new year?

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:42.000
You're still on my case about that?

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.800
I think I've more than paid my dues already.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:47.970
What else are you here for, then?

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.330
To hound me for New Year's money?

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:51.480
You're close.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:55.720
I want to go to the mainland. Help me out.

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:01.670
Then you need to go to 
the appropriate office and get a visa.

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:04.860
But you'll need to be registered 
as a demon before it'll be approved,

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.540
which would expose your identity.

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:09.780
That's why I came to ask you for help.

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:14.540
It'd be easy for you to get me off the island 
without all the inspections, right?

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:18.370
Even if I could do that,

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:21.700
I don't see why I'm obligated 
to do that for you.

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:24.000
Even if I told you 
someone's life depends on it?

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:28.660
Don't go poking around in the 
Lake Kannawa matter, Akatsuki Kojou.

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:32.150
No matter how much you're 
worried about your sister.

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:34.140
You know about it?

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:36.820
Then please, Natsuki-chan! 
You have to help me!

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:37.850
I refuse.

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:39.360
Why?!

00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:44.000
Do I need a reason to stop my student 
from breaking the law?

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:49.200
Fine. I get it.

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:50.430
Senpai?

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:53.360
It's okay, Natsuki-chan.

00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:57.160
Sorry to ask that of you 
without considering your position.

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:00.200
Senpai!

00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:02.990
Hold it, Akatsuki. Where are you going?

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:05.560
To ask someone else.

00:22:05.560 --> 00:22:06.400
No.

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:23.540
Natsuki-chan!

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:28.400
How many times must I tell you not to 
address your teacher with "chan"?

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:31.090
Senpai!

00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:34.050
Akatsuki Kojou...

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:37.300
I won't allow you to get to the mainland.
